# Old Hugo site (Firebase Hosting) → this one. Kept because the old URLs are in
# the wild: they are in Google's index, in the old sitemap, and in the RSS guids.
#
# Every canonical URL on the old site ended in a slash, and Hugo 301'd the
# slashless form to it. Both forms are listed rather than trusting the splat to
# catch the slashed one — the leaving-linedata post is the single highest-value
# redirect on the site and falling through to /blog would lose it.
#
# Static rules first: Cloudflare matches in order and warns when an exact rule
# sits below a splat that would shadow it.

# The only real post the old site ever published.
/posts/updates/leaving-linedata   /blog/leaving-linedata  301
/posts/updates/leaving-linedata/  /blog/leaving-linedata  301

# Feeds. Hugo named them index.xml, not rss.xml — /index.xml was the site feed
# and /posts/index.xml the section feed. Both were live and both had subscribers.
/index.xml        /rss.xml  301
/posts/index.xml  /rss.xml  301

# Hugo's client-side search: the Fuse.js index and the page that consumed it.
/index.json  /  301
/search      /  301
/search/     /  301

# Sections. Taxonomies are gone by design — this site does not have tags.
/posts        /blog    301
/posts/       /blog    301
/notes        /garden  301
/notes/       /garden  301
/tags         /blog    301
/tags/        /blog    301
/categories   /blog    301
/categories/  /blog    301

# Everything below those trees: individual taxonomy terms, pagination, anything
# the old catch-all rewrite happened to answer with a 200.
/posts/updates/*  /blog    301
/posts/*          /blog    301
/notes/*          /garden  301
/tags/*           /blog    301
/categories/*     /blog    301
